          "content": "a healthy body. Good health is essential for leading a happy life."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.124,
            0.743,
            0.167
          ],
          "content": "Which of the two foods you studied in Activity 3.9 could be labelled as junk food?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.206,
            0.627,
            0.393
          ],
          "content": "Packaged food items must have information about the nutrients on their cover. The information should list the amount of each nutrient. Sometimes, more nutrients are added to the food during processing (fortification) to improve its nutritional quality. Iodised salt and some baby foods are examples of fortified foods. The Food Safety and Standard Authority of India (FSSAI) is a government agency that regulates food quality in India."
        },
        {
